.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/src/webdist
assets
deploy
*.md
*.bat
*.cmd
lib

# The Rust core's build trees (rust-core plan T23c, QA PG-5): core/target alone is 1-2 GB, and a host-built
# .node (win32 on a Windows host) must never reach a Linux build stage. Dockerfile.nvidia and Dockerfile.amd build
# the Linux binary in their own Rust stage; the test images get it in dist/native/, re-included below.
turbollm/core/target
turbollm/core/fixtures/gguf/.corpus-cache
turbollm/core/bindings/android/**/build
turbollm/core/bindings/android/**/.cxx
turbollm/core/bindings/android/.gradle
turbollm/core/bindings/node/*.node

# Dockerfile.test builds turbollm/dist on the HOST first, then COPYs it in,
# rather than bundling in-container (that OOM-crashed the 1.9 GiB test VM —
# see Dockerfile.test's header comment). Everything else stays excluded:
# node_modules is still always installed fresh in-container (a host
# node_modules would carry host-OS native bindings into a Linux image), and
# the other Dockerfiles' own multi-stage builds are unaffected since they
# never reference the host's turbollm/dist at all.
!turbollm/dist
!turbollm/dist/**
!turbollm/src/webdist
!turbollm/src/webdist/**